\begin{align*}
\sqrt{xy} &= 3b^{b+1}, \\
\log_b (x^{\log_b y}) + \log_b (y^{\log_b x}) &= 6b^5.
\end{align*}

Find the value of $b$ so that the lines with these equations are perpendicular:
\begin{align*}
y &= 3x - 7 \\
8y + bx = 16.
\end{align*}

Let \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
3x^2 - 5 & \text{if } x \le 3, \\
bx + 6 & \text{if } x > 3.
